- When VISCOSITY_OK becomes TRUE: enable the timer
- When VISCOSITY_OK stays TRUE and timer.Q becomes TRUE: viscosityValid = TRUE
- When VISCOSITY_OK becomes FALSE: disable timer, viscosityValid = FALSE immediately

The implementation needs to ensure that when VISCOSITY_OK goes TRUE, the timer starts immediately. On subsequent scans, once the timer completes, viscosityValid activates. If VISCOSITY_OK drops, the timer resets and viscosityValid deactivates right away.

There's also a critical safety requirement: the emergency stop must disable VFD_RUN immediately and clear any pending debounce state.

For runtime accumulation, I need to accumulate using the actual invocation interval (CycleTime) while VFD_RUN is active, preserving the value when stopped. The 500-hour maintenance threshold converts to 1,800,000,000 milliseconds, so I should check if PUMP_RUNTIME_ACC >= LTIME#500h using TON.Q semantics where the output triggers when elapsed time meets or exceeds the preset.

