For the contract rules, the pump run output is a direct function of the emergency stop and viscosity conditions—it activates when both are satisfied and resets immediately when either condition fails. The maintenance due flag similarly tracks accumulated runtime but doesn't directly control the pump output. The safety permissive VFD_RUN is governed by PASTE_E_STOP_NC and viscosity validity, with the E-stop providing immediate priority override. VFD_RUN activates when both safety conditions are met and remains active as long as they stay true, with the E-stop serving as the primary reset mechanism. Once VFD_RUN is enabled, runtime accumulates based on cycle time, and maintenance becomes due after 500 hours of operation—this is purely informational and doesn't affect the safety logic. Initialization sets all outputs to their default OFF state at power-up.

